<section class="bg-white py-12 lg:py-24 overflow-hidden">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">Methodology</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600">
        The process is designed for immediate clarity on whether a project should advance into deeper diligence. It does not validate for the sake of completion; it gates for decision quality.
        <br/><br/>
        <strong>This is decision-gating analysis, not certification or compliance validation.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="relative border-l-2 border-slate-200 ml-4 lg:ml-8 space-y-16">
      <div class="relative pl-8 lg:pl-12">
        <div class="absolute -left-[9px] top-2 w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-slate-900 ring-4 ring-white"></div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">1. Public Data Risk Detection</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-2xl">
          Initial diagnostic using only public information: environmental and planning records, interconnection disclosures, public technical materials, climate exposure, and jurisdiction-specific public filings. No data room access. No NDA.
          The project footprint is mapped against known technical and execution failure modes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative pl-8 lg:pl-12">
        <div class="absolute -left-[9px] top-2 w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-slate-400 ring-4 ring-white"></div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">2. Silence Identification & Classification</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mb-4">
          All relevant data points are classified to prevent false confidence:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-600 mb-6">
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-slate-900">
               <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-green-500 rounded-full"></span> Verified:
            </div>
            <p class="pl-4 text-slate-500">Confirmed by independent tangible evidence (e.g., stamped engineering drawings, published interconnection study results).</p>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-slate-900">
               <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span> Assumed:
            </div>
            <p class="pl-4 text-slate-500">Based on industry standard practice but unverified by project-specific documentation. Flagged explicitly as risk.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-red-600">
               <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-red-500 rounded-full"></span> Critical Silence:
            </div>
            <p class="pl-4 text-slate-500">Material omissions that undermine technical confidence, execution viability, or insurance positioning.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-sm border border-slate-100 mb-4">
             <p class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm mb-2">Examples of Critical Silences:</p>
             <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-sm text-slate-600 space-y-1">
                <li>Missing thermal derating disclosure → summer performance assumptions remain unvalidated</li>
                <li>Absent fire propagation or safety evidence → insurance positioning remains uncertain</li>
                <li>Undisclosed logistics or structural constraints → delivery path may be materially exposed</li>
                <li>Unclear permitting dependency → project schedule confidence is overstated</li>
             </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="relative pl-8 lg:pl-12">
        <div class="absolute -left-[9px] top-2 w-4 h-4 rounded-full bg-slate-400 ring-4 ring-white"></div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">3. Decision Gating</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mb-4">
          The result is a formal technical recommendation: <strong>GO</strong>, <strong>CONDITIONAL NO-GO</strong>, or <strong>NO-GO</strong>.
        </p>
        
        <div class="bg-slate-50 border-l-4 border-slate-900 p-4">
             <p class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">This is a technical gate, not a certification service.</p>
             <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-4">
                If the public record does not support confidence, the report identifies exactly what must be clarified before deeper diligence proceeds.
             </p>
             <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">
                If public records already show material uncertainty, you avoid wasting diligence budget on premature escalation.
             </p>
             <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-sm text-slate-600 mt-2 space-y-1">
                <li>site visits before documentary viability is established</li>
                <li>data-room and legal process before core questions are framed</li>
                <li>full diligence on a project that may still be technically under-disclosed</li>
             </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
